  "Spectrum is licensed by the Department of Electronic Communications (DEC), under the Deputy Ministry of Research, Innovation and Digital Policy. OCECPR regulates the market but does not publish spectrum holdings.",
  "800/900/1800/2100/2600 MHz amounts come from the DEC renewal consultation (Feb 2023, Tables 1–2). The Nov 2023 decision (THE 4/2023) renewed the Cyta, Epic and PrimeTel 900/1800/2100 rights and the Cyta and Epic 800/2600 rights to 21 Jun 2029. The DEC register (April 2025) confirms all these authorisations expire 2029-06-21.",
  "The 700 MHz and 3.6 GHz holdings are incomplete. DEC's register confirms that all four operators hold 5G authorisations, but the per-operator lot counts from the 2021 auction were not found in a regulator document. Only Cyta's 2×10 MHz and 100 MHz (Wikipedia, citing TeleGeography) are sourced; the other operators are shown with the guaranteed minimum.",
  "The DEC register lists no mmWave, 1.5 GHz or 2.3 GHz authorisations.",
  "Operator colours are approximate brand colours."
